ary facilities near Sabah have revived questions over Malaysia's non-aligned foreign policy.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Jaishankar offers help to end war in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd7ecbda496f610ca6cfe6a33c4b6f1ea9b4910458c777d6a94939017a4e7850</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T11:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-jaishankar-offers-help-to-end-war-in-ukraine/live-78815659--a0b97c3b0026.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-jaishankar-offers-help-to-end-war-in-ukraine/live-78815659?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Foreign Minister S. Jaishankar says India is prepared to assist efforts to end the war in Ukraine, as the foreign minister visits Kyiv. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India rejects Hague ruling on Indus waters: What's next?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cb9e8cfe4ea53e86e197738fcdccbc10d6497edbf9ced597a16511c9efee90d</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T13:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-rejects-hague-ruling-on-indus-waters-what-s-next/a-78753249--f1f03d136f38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-rejects-hague-ruling-on-indus-waters-what-s-next/a-78753249?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">By rejecting an international arbitration panel's ruling, New Delhi has cast fresh doubt on the future of the 1960 Indus Waters Treaty.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can communities be proteced from melting glaciers?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5b4eb5d11de0c9ea69658784220eee1dcbd4526cfe9c2f4321b1723baee411f</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775--1f4c55c04fcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-communities-be-proteced-from-melting-glaciers/a-78615775?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising temperatures are increasing the risk of floods and avalanches in mountain regions. The disaster in Nepal and Tibet shows the urgent need for solutions, and the tools that could help save lives.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Bangladesh join the Mecca defense alliance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e49f12e46a915dece598cacf3f2aec59d928ae8643046f2f7a7e8c78a82dcc0</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944--650fbd31b54b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Bangladesh weighs the risks of signing the Mecca Joint Defense Agreement, experts warn that such a move could complicate relations with neighboring India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How China buried Tibet flood images after Nepal disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:782140b2ef719d6a7f3b8a3661ea7a320d177ac1fdc821884dc68ba85a42ad85</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-china-buried-tibet-flood-images-after-nepal-disaster/a-78576472--7e7c26844487.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-china-buried-tibet-flood-images-after-nepal-disaster/a-78576472?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In Tibet, a digital crackdown followed the deadly flood that has devastated communities along the China-Nepal border. Censors erased viral footage while Chinese state media flooded platforms with official content.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>With multilateralism in decline, what's next for the world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a81d8ffc03856ab4acaad6763dddaa704ba9629e65fec8283543140779df579f</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T11:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/with-multilateralism-in-decline-what-s-next-for-the-world/a-78555977--8df5725f7fb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/with-multilateralism-in-decline-what-s-next-for-the-world/a-78555977?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The global political architecture is shifting, partly as a result of the actions of US President Donald Trump. As nations search for a new world order, some may gain influence and power, while others have much to lose.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Inside the sea cucumber smuggling boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3d3c09316d40f86da8db05f229a41e1888fdd1e826a3427168f63e03f1bcaa7</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662--0b2701be2732.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quiet multimillion‑dollar black market is exploding across the Indian Ocean, driven by one unlikely animal: the sea cucumber.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry></feed>
